A||||2||wallmic||Tires for winter driving??
Z||000000||wallmic||08-17-99||08:04 PM||||Anyone have any recommendations for tire sizes for winter driving in snow?  I was considering narrower tires.  I have a 85 GT with P215-60R14's.
Z||000001||lowCG||08-17-99||08:24 PM||||Blizzak's;work on glare ice,and that's good enough for me.For a size,I'd go for something a little more tractor-like than your original size,maybe 195/70 14.<br>These tires will give a sense of security you've never had before in foul conditions,however,this could possibly set you up for a bad one if you're not just as careful as you were with,say only studded tires.
Z||000002||batboy||08-17-99||09:57 PM||||My experience has shown that nothing really works well on ice except maybe studded tires. But for snow, a narrower tire with an agressive open lug tread works great. Of course, those kind of tires will "sing" to you on dry pavement at highway speed. A good snow tire the size that LowCG mention is a nice compromise. Plus, as with all adverse weather conditions, slowing down and driving defensively helps wonders too.
